# Validation Test Case 3: Activity Failure Scenario

## Input
```json
{
  "templateId": "intentional-failure-test",
  "variables": {
    "featureName": "failure-test",
    "shouldFail": true,
    "failureType": "validation"
  },
  "reason": "Test MCP data flow for failed activities",
  "expectedImpulseCount": 3,
  "expectedComponentCount": 0
}
```

## Expected Output
```json
{
  "pass": true,
  "results": {
    "activityExecution": {
      "exists": true,
      "hasCorrectTemplate": true,
      "hasMetrics": true,
      "hasImpulsesUsed": true,
      "hasComponentChanges": false,
      "impulsesUsedCount": 3,
      "componentsChangedCount": 0
    },
    "impulseUsage": {
      "recordsCreated": true,
      "recordCount": 3,
      "linkedToExecution": true
    },
    "impulseRegistry": {
      "updatedSuccessRates": true,
      "impulseCount": 3
    },
    "mcpPayload": {
      "captured": true,
      "hasImpulsesUsed": true,
      "hasComponentChanges": false
    }
  },
  "actual": {
    "impulsesUsed": [
      {"impulse_id": "test-impulse-1", "was_useful": false},
      {"impulse_id": "test-impulse-2", "was_useful": false},
      {"impulse_id": "test-impulse-3", "was_useful": false}
    ]
  },
  "errors": []
}
```

## Test Description
Validates that failed activities still transmit learning data correctly.
Verifies impulses are marked as not useful (was_useful: false) for failed executions.
Tests that failure doesn't break data flow - learning from failures is critical.

## Success Criteria
- Activity fails as expected (validation error)
- Impulses still tracked despite failure
- All impulses marked with was_useful: false
- No component changes (activity failed before modifications)
- Impulse registry still updated with failure data
- MCP payload correctly transmits failure context
